------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3) LEAD DISTRIBUTION (AUTOMATED SPLIT)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NOTE
- Use split_recipients_5.py to pull from source, split evenly into 5 files, and optionally remove from source.
- Use `--append` to ADD to existing recipient files (recommended for your workflow).
- Without `--append`, the script REPLACES/rewrites the recipient files.

PULL 100 FROM leads_prechecked.csv -> recipients_sendgrid_1..5 (20 each) AND REMOVE
python3 split_recipients_5.py \
  --src leads_prechecked.csv \
  --dst recipients_sendgrid_1.csv recipients_sendgrid_2.csv recipients_sendgrid_3.csv recipients_sendgrid_4.csv recipients_sendgrid_5.csv \
  --count 100 \
  --remove \
  --append

PULL ALL LEADS FROM leads_prechecked.csv -> recipients_1..5 (EVEN SPLIT) AND REMOVE
python3 split_recipients_5.py \
  --src leads_prechecked.csv \
  --dst recipients_1.csv recipients_2.csv recipients_3.csv recipients_4.csv recipients_5.csv \
  --count 0 \
  --remove \
  --append


DISTRIBUTE ALL REMAINING FROM leads_prechecked.csv -> recipients_1..5 (NO REMOVE)
python3 split_recipients_5.py \
  --src leads_prechecked.csv \
  --dst recipients_1.csv recipients_2.csv recipients_3.csv recipients_4.csv recipients_5.csv \
  --count 0 \
  --append

OPTIONAL: KEEP windellejcr@gmail.com ON TOP OF EACH recipients_1..5 FILE (ONE-TIME TEST)
python3 split_recipients_5.py \
  --src leads_prechecked.csv \
  --dst recipients_1.csv recipients_2.csv recipients_3.csv recipients_4.csv recipients_5.csv \
  --count 1000 \
  --remove \
  --append \
  --keep-top-email windellejcr@gmail.com \
  --keep-top-name Windelle \
  --keep-top-title Test

